\section{Stratos-Core: Real-Time Atmospheric Domination Engine}
\subsection{System Overview}
Stratos-Core is a unified atmospheric control and simulation architecture
integrating astrometric ingestion, multispectral satellite fusion, global
fluid dynamics, radiative forcing invariants, microphysical substrates, and
closed-loop intervention control. The system operates under strict
mathematical invariants ensuring stability, conservation, and zero drift.

\subsection{Astrometric Ingestion Pipeline}
Real-time telemetry is ingested from multispectral and hyperspectral
satellite arrays, including GOES-R, Sentinel-5P, and auxiliary atmospheric
sensors. Data streams include:
\begin{itemize}
    \item aerosol optical depth (AOD),
    \item greenhouse gas concentration profiles,
    \item shortwave/longwave radiative flux,
    \item stratospheric temperature and humidity layers.
\end{itemize}

Global grid resolution:
\[
0.05^\circ \times 0.05^\circ,\quad 128\ \text{vertical layers}.
\]

Telemetry ingestion rate:
\[
1.2\ \text{TB/sec}.
\]

